 Q("Categories","Which of these is a medical embedded system?","A pacemaker",["A washing machine","A traffic light","A car engine controller"],"An insulin pump is another example."),
 Q("Categories","Which of these is an automotive embedded system?","An anti-lock brake controller",["An insulin pump","A dishwasher","A factory floor sensor"],"The engine control unit is another."),
 Q("Categories","Which of these is an industrial embedded system?","A factory floor sensor",["A microwave oven","A pacemaker","An anti-lock brake controller"],"Industrial systems run machines and processes."),
 Q("Categories","Which of these is a household embedded system?","A washing machine",["A pacemaker","A factory floor sensor","An engine control unit"],"Microwaves and thermostats count too."),
 Q("Appliance","In a washing machine's control board, what is a sensor?","An input that measures something, like the water level",["An output that moves something, like a drain pump","The program that runs the whole wash cycle","The chip that holds the cycle program"],"Sensors are inputs and actuators are outputs."),
 Q("Appliance","Which of these is an actuator in a washing machine?","The drain pump",["The water level sensor","The lid switch","The temperature sensor"],"An actuator physically does something."),
 Q("Appliance","Which of these is a sensor in a washing machine?","The door or lid switch",["The water inlet valve","The drain pump","The heating element"],"It reads whether the lid is shut."),
 Q("Numbers","About how many embedded computers do engineers commonly estimate in a modern car?","Somewhere between 70 and 150 or more",["Exactly one large central computer","Only two or three, for the brakes","Over one million for each car"],"They are dozens of tiny, single-purpose computers."),
 Q("Sorting","Which of these is a general-purpose computer?","A Chromebook",["A digital kitchen scale","A pacemaker","A car's anti-lock brake controller"],"The others are built for one fixed job."),
